id: pm-rl-release-gate
title: Release readiness behind PM_RELEASE_APPROVED
description: "Prepare daily OIDC publishing behind one repository approval variable. Verify metadata, allowlisted packed files, privacy, regression checks, npm and Bun release gates. The owner performs the first npm publish and trusted-publisher setup; keep approval unset."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-25T23:22:14.351Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T10:35:55.494Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-27T10:12:37.865Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-27T05:09:20.000Z"
author: codex-agent
resolution: "Deliver release-ready daily OIDC publishing guarded by explicit repository approval and canonical-repository write conditions, with verified package metadata and packed consumers."
expected_result: "Automated publication requires main, the canonical repository, PM_RELEASE_APPROVED and tokenless OIDC provenance; package metadata and documented local first publication remain correct."
actual_result: "Current-main release-approval and related focused checks pass through pinned pm. Inspected workflow, manifest and README satisfy readiness requirements; the merged PR retains complete final npm/Bun and packed inventory/privacy receipts. Owner publication and trust decisions remain unchanged."
comments[20]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T23:22:17.804Z",codex-agent,"Normalize daily scheduling and PM_RELEASE_APPROVED job gates while preserving release decisions, generated changelogs and release notes. Verify OIDC publishing without a stored npm token, manifest metadata, packed allowlists and private-data scans. No open homepage/author PR was found during orientation. No publishing, trust setup, approval variable changes or merges are authorized."
  "2026-10-25T23:22:58.649Z",codex-agent,"Normalize daily scheduling and PM_RELEASE_APPROVED job gates while preserving release decisions, generated changelogs and release notes. Verify OIDC publishing without a stored npm token, manifest metadata, packed allowlists and private-data scans. No open homepage/author PR was found during orientation. No publishing, trust setup, approval variable changes or merges are authorized."
  "2026-10-25T23:23:39.217Z",codex-agent,"Normalize daily scheduling and PM_RELEASE_APPROVED job gates while preserving release decisions, generated changelogs and release notes. Verify OIDC publishing without a stored npm token, manifest metadata, packed allowlists and private-data scans. No open homepage/author PR was found during orientation. No publishing, trust setup, approval variable changes or merges are authorized."
  "2026-10-26T00:08:31.917Z",codex-agent,"Calendar-release inspection found that changelog:full and release:notes fixed the bootstrap date instead of deriving it from the selected package version. Replaced that fixed override with --date-from-version so later calendar releases retain matching changelog dates. The release workflow already derives its selected date and retains the existing decision logic. The calendar regression fails with the original scripts and passes 1/1 with version-derived dates."
  "2026-10-26T00:17:55.466Z",codex-agent,"Pack verification: npm pack --dry-run --json and the actual npm pack --ignore-scripts artifact agree on 216 allowlisted files (dist: 164; docs: 28; examples: 17; root files: 7). Every packed member was scanned for absolute home paths, npm/GitHub/cloud tokens, private keys, hosted-data locations, private addresses and historical owner email addresses: PASS with zero matches. Regression proof: five independent workflow mutations (approval, provenance, token environment, daily schedule and OR bypass) plus the original manifest each fail the new contract check; restored contract passes 4/4. The linked test also passes through pm test --run --progress. Next gates: npm run release:check and bun run release:check with isolated HOME and Git configuration."
  "2026-10-26T00:49:46.117Z",codex-agent,"The first local npm gate hit the existing 300-second SIGKILL receipt-boundary test timeout under shared CPU contention. The release-readiness changes do not modify the controller or test budget. Inspecting and retrying that exact crash scenario unchanged; no timeout, source coverage threshold or case is being removed or raised. Full gate results remain pending and are not recorded as passing."
  "2026-10-26T00:55:11.213Z",codex-agent,"Opening the release-readiness PR so isolated GitHub CI can exercise both unchanged full release gates while local verification continues. The local npm run reached one 300-second crash-boundary timeout under shared host load; it is not counted as a passing gate. The same exact scenario is being retried without coverage to characterize the failure, and the complete gate will be retried with unchanged budgets. npm/Bun CI must pass before readiness is claimed."
  "2026-10-26T02:24:21.017Z",codex-agent,"Required complete npm run release:check and bun run release:check both PASS in isolated GitHub CI at 112788d6a1f6a270693770ece78df35e3f0e39cd. Main suite counts: npm 1026/1026, Bun 1026/1026; every required matrix job succeeded. Evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/40251686818. The first shared-host npm attempt exceeded the unchanged 300-second crash-boundary budget. The exact focused retry passed 1/1 in that budget. Later duplicate local work was stopped after complete isolated CI passed; no failed or interrupted local attempt is counted as a pass. No timeout, case, threshold or dependency pin was changed. Packed artifact allowlist/privacy checks and linked regressions passed. Final tracker evidence is being committed and CI will recheck that final head. Keep the item in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-27T00:12:35.947Z",codex-agent,"Review follow-up: preserve existing release-readiness work and merged main changes. Remove automatic release-workflow enablement; the orchestrator enables disabled schedules after merge. Require the canonical repository at job level for every write-permission or publishing job in the affected workflows, alongside the existing approval and branch conditions. Prove guard, approval, provenance and token regressions independently, then wait for complete npm and Bun CI on the pushed head."
  "2026-10-27T00:13:53.208Z",codex-agent,"Packed-artifact verification: 216 allowlisted files; dry-run and actual archive agree, and every packed member has zero private-data findings. Local project health passes with extensions disabled; globally installed extension version skew is outside this package."
  "2026-10-27T00:13:58.179Z",codex-agent,"Fork-exclusion revert proof: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/release-approval.test.ts passes 6/6. Independently reverting each job repository guard, reverting all repository guards, allowing an OR bypass, removing approval or provenance, injecting a synthetic npm token environment, adding an unguarded CI write job, inheriting CI write permissions, adding a read-permission CI publisher, and restoring automatic setup all fail (each command exits nonzero; 10 independent mutations rejected). Restoring the workflows passes 6/6. Linked pm tests, test typecheck where present and lint pass. Canonical-repository checks include inherited permissions. Disabled release workflows remain for the orchestrator to enable after merge; no live settings or publishing were changed."
  "2026-10-27T01:00:09.965Z",codex-agent,"Final CI log inspection found that the coverage runner uses an explicit test list and does not execute the release-approval or calendar regressions. Put both focused files directly at the start of release:check so npm and Bun enforce the workflow contract before the full source suite. Add a regression for this entrypoint connection and prove that removing only the connection fails. Keep the full source inventory, thresholds, dependencies and workflow guards unchanged."
  "2026-10-27T01:01:03.145Z",codex-agent,"Release entrypoint wiring proof: the combined workflow/calendar command passes 7/7. Restoring only the previous release:check script, while retaining the regression, fails on the missing focused-contract entrypoint; restoring the prefix passes 7/7. Both direct npm and Bun release:check now execute these checks before the unchanged full 1026-test source suite. Existing repository, approval, provenance and token mutation proofs remain valid. Linked pm tests, test typecheck and lint pass; complete CI must verify the new pushed head."
  "2026-10-27T01:55:05.208Z",codex-agent,"A newer main update landed while final CI was running. Integrate that upstream commit, preserving the release workflow and regression bytes exactly. Refresh pinned dependencies from the merged lockfile, rerun linked workflow checks, regenerate the changelog and scan the refreshed actual package before verifying complete npm and Bun CI on the new merge head. Existing independent revert proofs remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-27T01:55:30.824Z",codex-agent,"Main integration checks pass: linked workflow regressions, changelog currency, and the actual tarball allowlist/private-data scan (216 files, zero findings). Release workflow and approval regression source bytes are unchanged, including direct release-check entrypoint enforcement where applicable. The new main feature or toolchain update is retained; full npm and Bun CI must pass on the new merge head."
  "2026-10-27T03:17:54.493Z",codex-agent,"Independent re-review found the contract covered only release and CI files, missing CodeQL security-events writes, owner-only Dependabot guards and reusable workflow callers. Extend canonical-repository guards to every effectively write-enabled job in every workflow file. Replace regex workflow parsing with a pinned YAML parser, generic permission inheritance and negative fixtures for this full class. Correct local publishing documentation, preserve earlier readiness work, prove source reverts and wait for npm/Bun CI on every final head."
  "2026-10-27T03:55:27.617Z",codex-agent,"Whole-workflow contract passes 30/30 using the pinned YAML parser. It scans every YAML workflow, resolves aliases/flow maps, applies job permission overrides or workflow inheritance, and recognizes any scope with write plus write-all, including reusable callers. Negative fixtures cover CodeQL, owner-only/wrong-repository Dependabot, inherited writes, reusable calls, write-all, future scopes, missing publication approval/provenance, provenance overrides, token environments, OR/negation bypasses and discovery of a new workflow in a non-Git directory. Behavioural revert proof: all 13 independent mutations fail with assertion failures: each write job loses only its repository guard, owner-only/OR guards return, approval/provenance disappear, a synthetic token environment is added, file discovery is narrowed back to release/CI, permission matching returns to a scope allowlist, or inheritance is removed. Restoring the implementation passes 30/30. Linked pm tests and the repository's defined typecheck, lint and duplication checks pass. Maintainer local publishing is authenticated and checked, with no approval-variable hold; the variable gates automated GitHub releases."
  "2026-10-27T10:12:30.062Z",codex-agent,"Closure audit of current main: Inspected current-main daily release workflow, manifest and maintainer documentation. The YAML contract scans every workflow and enforces the exact canonical repository on write-enabled jobs, main and PM_RELEASE_APPROVED on publishers, OIDC provenance, public npm access and no npm token environments. Negative fixtures cover inherited permissions, reusable callers, future scopes, aliases and wrong-repository/OR bypasses; plain-directory workflow discovery is covered. The merged PR records allowlisted actual/dry-run tarball parity, privacy scans, real npm/Bun packed consumers, behavioral revert proofs and final complete npm/Bun CI. Initial publication, trust setup and approval remain owner operations. Delivered by PR #108, merge commit 9b90a792d58adde7dc369438007af2ab0ed432ac, merged_at 2026-10-27T05:09:20Z. Focused verification follows; full npm and Bun release gates are delegated to PR CI for this tracker-only change."
  "2026-10-27T10:12:36.276Z",codex-agent,"Verified current main with `node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/release-approval.test.ts test/release-calendar.test.ts` via the pinned pm linked runner: PASS. Observed test counts: tests=31, pass=31, fail=0, cancelled=0, skipped=0, todo=0. Current-main release-approval and related focused checks pass through pinned pm. Inspected workflow, manifest and README satisfy readiness requirements; the merged PR retains complete final npm/Bun and packed inventory/privacy receipts. Owner publication and trust decisions remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-27T10:35:55.494Z",codex-agent,"Closure validation: health retains the same legacy provenance advisory as untouched main 9b90a792d58adde7dc369438007af2ab0ed432ac: provenance_value_domain_invalid:claude-code:role:single_digit:138. Existing item pm-rl-9uz4 owns this advisory. Strict health is not clean; the original history bytes remain unchanged. Default health additionally reports the existing global extension version skew. No history repair or dependency change is performed."
